<%# locals: (offer:) %>
<%# What making the rule would do, which depends on its text and Account, so the filing form asks for this again as either is edited (the sweep-preview controller sets the frame's address): it says when a Filing rule with that text and Account (or any Account) exists, which is updated in place and not made again, and how many other unfiled bank transactions it would file or ignore, with a box to do that, ticked to start with. A text that isn't one a rule can have has no count, and says why. The text as the rule keeps it, without its numbers and symbols, comes with every answer, hidden, and the sweep-preview controller puts it in the sentence under "Always file like this" when the frame loads, so that the cleaning is only ever done by the server. %>
<% existing = offer.existing_rule %>
<turbo-frame id="filing-rule-preview" class="block space-y-4" aria-live="polite" data-sweep-preview-target="frame" data-action="turbo:frame-load->sweep-preview#showCleanedText">
  <span hidden data-sweep-preview-target="cleaned"><%= offer.normalized_text %></span>
  <% if existing %>
    <p class="font-medium">Updates the Filing rule for '<%= existing.text %>'<%= " in #{existing.account.name}" if existing.account %>, which <%= existing.effect %> now.</p>
  <% end %>
  <% if offer.valid_text? %>
    <%= render "filing_rules/sweep_option", scope: "filing[rule]", sweep: offer.sweep_preview, checked: offer.sweep, others: true %>
  <% else %>
    <p class="text-base-content/70">The text has to be at least 3 characters once numbers and symbols are ignored, and part of this bank transaction's description.</p>
  <% end %>
</turbo-frame>
